WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.090
We will talk about what will save the world,
and we can never save the world without politics.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:14.400
So what's your take on the anger amongst people
against the political class?

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.990
Well, in Lincoln's day there was even anger
against the political class, and Lincoln himself,

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:28.019
in one of his early speeches as a young man,
attacked politicians, saying 'I know', to

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:34.770
his audience, 'that you'll understand that,
because I am a politician myself.'

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:42.070
So there's always been this strain, particularly
in American politics, of scepticism about

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.300
politicians.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:53.370
We're in one of these periods where there
is such scepticism, but it runs deeper.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:01:02.000
It's not as deep as the crisis that occurred
in the 1920s and 1930s, which turned into

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.530
a profound crisis of democracy.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:11.250
We may be on the eve of such a thing, where
people feel that democracy itself is not only

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:22.140
inadequate, but also the obstacle to resolving
their problems, and that order is more important

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.140
to them.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.570
I don't believe that that'll ever happen in
America, but we have such a figure in Donald

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:38.750
Trump, who exploits disorder in order to claim
to be the authoritarian figure to impose order.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:45.290
This is a profound question, beyond the United
States, that affects the West.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.610
It affects both conservative parties and social-democratic
parties.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:55.540
In the United States, it particularly affects
the Republican Party.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:01.610
The Democratic Party always had problems.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:08.280
While it showed a split in its primary between
Bernie Sanders and Hillary Clinton, it is

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.569
now much more unified than the Republican
Party.

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:16.939
We will see what the outcome is, and we will
know it when we appear at the conference.

00:02:16.939 --> 00:02:24.950
But there is still a problem - an intellectual
problem, a problem of ideas, a problem of

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:31.519
culture, particularly in the European social-democratic
tradition.

00:02:31.519 --> 00:02:42.829
I believe this is not the problem in the United
States, for American liberalism.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:47.840
We have many different traditions to draw
upon that are quite diverse.

